2. Core Governance Invariants Re-Verified
Review Flow & Gating (ProposalReviewFlowPolicy.md, ReviewCommitGovernancePolicy.md):
Proposal-first invariant (RULE-LCM-001); normal cycle suggestions halt at Gate 1; BUG items execute in DOIT mode directly to Gate 2.
Gate 2 (Beyond Compare visual diff) is non-circumventable for code/tools/specs across all items (RULE-REV-001), with transparent junction traversal via FollowSymLinks (RULE-REV-008).
There are two exceptions to this rule 
1. The user can explicitly INSTRUCT (IMMEDIATELY, FORCE) to go into the Implementation Phase without confirming the review.
2. System has detected a BUG that impedes the intended Flow in a critical manner. This is especially the case when the task would lead to a loop/recursion (which the user can't avoid or fix). There must be no more than 2 attempts to resolve the Issue.
In either case, the fact must be logged in the BUG or CRP.
Dual-commit synchronization with LCM_Inventory (RULE-LCM-005).
Discrete commands: Proceed (single discrete status pulse), do (activates DOIT velocity), COMPLETE (records visual review, commits locally), PUBLISH / PUSH (preflighted lockstep remote dispatch with auto-reset to LCM ON and Testing ON).
Mandatory SemVer auto-increment per change (RULE-REV-007).
Proposal bundle architecture (docs/Proposals/CRP-<nnn>-[Slug]/ or BUG-<nnn>-[Slug]/) with post-push directory purge and Git object retrieval (RULE-LCM-020).
Atomic single-edit consolidation per turn with zero editor diff stacking (RULE-LCM-022).
PowerShell Standards (PowerShellStandardsPolicy.md, PowerShellRules.md):
PS7 (pwsh) exclusive workspace-wide; intermediate code parity (RULE-PS-019).
@(...) wrapping for scalar collection access under StrictMode Latest (RULE-PS-001).
Colon-safe string interpolation ${var}: to prevent scope parsing collisions (RULE-PS-003, RULE-PS-015).
Single-quoted here-strings for inline pwsh -Command blocks (RULE-PS-016).
Interactive desktop dispatch via Invoke-InteractiveDesktop.ps1 for Session 1 GUI routing (RULE-PS-011).
Efficiency & System Boundaries (MethodEfficiencyPolicy.md, ElevationPolicy.md, SubsystemGovernancePolicy.md):
Auto-acceptance of mechanical evidence/logs with zero-test cascades (RULE-EFF-001, RULE-EFF-002).
High-speed search dispatch via Search-Everything.ps1 or Everything HTTP REST (port 8080) and rg.exe (RULE-EFF-007).
Tool discovery strictly via tool_catalog.json first (RULE-EFF-008).
Zero speculative relative pathing (RULE-ENV-003).
Privilege interception routing (RULE-ELEV-006) and elevated console persistence with -NoExit / /k (RULE-ELEV-005).
Subsystem read-only central registry invariant (RULE-SUB-007) and JIT ephemeral write auth (RULE-SUB-004).
